  $ chi \( theta \) chi \( - theta \) thin P_Y \( d w \) P_F \( d v \) = P_Y \( d w \) P_F \( d v \) $
  on such patches. Nonzero ordered rectangles exist by Lemma 105; hence $\| chi \( theta \) \| = 1$. Since $chi$ is a probability characteristic function, it is the characteristic function of a point mass. Its scalar is a positive constant raised to the imaginary power. Simultaneous source transport and the pairing covariance give $C \( Y \, F \) = c k_S \( y_(i^(*)) \, x_i \)$.
